      "writtenOn": "2013-03-23T13:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think we need to be clean one way the other.  The approach we are taking here (which I support) is that all we are doing on token validation is enumerating the contents of the token created earlier, for which the token_id has been supplied.\n\nget_token_data() is currently called for both the new token case (by create_token() ) as well as the the token validation case (by  recreate_token() ).  I\u0027d suggest that the best way to implement the change we want is for recreate_token to NOT call get_token_data(), since, as you indicate, we will have set up nearly all the token data anyway.  I think all we need is some tinkering with date expires/issues data.  Then it is clear that get_token_data(), and its sub-functions, have one task to build the token the first time on creation.  We can then remove the bailout checks you have added to these sub-functions.",
      "revId": "c6d579e6f7a3e6154a0cfad86cc08775bf86587e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
